tumor_1_gross_ete:
The specimen is received in formalin labeled with the patient's name, medical record number, labeled "total thyroidectomy with central compartment, stitch right superior" on the container and consists of a total thyroid (5.6 x 3.2 x 1.4 cm, 13 g-total; 
2.8 x 2.0 x 1.4 cm-left lobe; 2.7 x 2.1 x 1.2 cm-right lobe; 2.2 x 1.6-0.5 cm-isthmus) with attached adipose tissue at the inferior isthmus (1.4 a 1.2 x 0.6 cm). There is a stitch designating the right superior lobe. 
Sectioning reveals a tan-red, cystic and solid lesion (1.4 x 1.2 x 1.1 cm) in the left inferior lobe.  The right lobe is unremarkable.

GROSS DESCRIPTION:
Part A is received in formalin labeled "Jeffery Tolnar, 06/06/1963," and "thyroid suture to right lobe."  It consists of a 23.0 gram total thyroidectomy specimen consisting of a 4.8 x 2.5 x 1.9 cm right lobe, 3.5 x 2.5 x 2.0 cm isthmus, and 4.1 x 1.7 x
0.8 cm left lobe.  Present on the isthmus is a 1.1 x 0.6 x 0.4 cm pyramidal lobe.  A suture is present on the right superior pole.   The surface of the thyroid is tan-pink and glistening with areas of adhesions.  The right lobe is inked black, the
isthmus is inked green, and the left lobe is inked blue.  No parathyroid glands are grossly identified.  Sectioning reveals a 2.4 x 2.1 x 1.7 cm circumscribed tan-pink papillary mass within the isthmus which abuts the green-inked capsule.  Present within
 the left inferior pole is a 0.5 cm calcified nodule.  The remaining cut surface consists of tan-red glistening parenchyma.  Representative sections are submitted as follows:
A1-A9 - entire mass submitted sequentially from inferior to superior (A3 and A4 one complete cross-section, A5 and A6 one complete cross-section, A7 and A8 one complete cross-section);
A10 - calcified nodule within left inferior pole; following decalcification;
A11-A13 - representative left lobe submitted sequentially from inferior to superior;
A14-A15 - representative right lobe, submitted sequentially from inferior to superior.
VG/dl/seu

Specimen A is received fresh with patient's name and medical record number and consists of a total thyroidectomy specimen weighing 25.0 grams, measuring as follows: 

Right lobe  5.6 x 2.6 x 1.2 cm; 
Isthmus  1.3 x 0.7 cm; 
Left lobe  5.0 x 2.5 x 1.0 cm. The external surface is tan-grey and appears nodular. 

The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan-white well-delineated firm mass measuring 1.4 x 1.3 x 1.0 cm on the left lobe.  This mass is 0.1 cm both from the anterior and posterior margins.  The remainder of the thyroid parenchyma is tan-grey, 
smooth and appears spongy.  No other discrete lesions are identified.  Representative sections are submitted as follows.  Dictated by Abdul Samad, P.A. (ASCP)
